  "summary": "Traditional painted furniture from Moravia featuring floral patterns, geometric designs, and symbolic motifs.",
  "description": "Moravian painted furniture includes cupboards, chests, and cabinets decorated with intricate floral patterns, geometric borders, and symbolic motifs in vibrant colors including red, blue, yellow, and green. This folk art tradition emerged in Moravian villages as a way to decorate functional household items, with designs reflecting local agricultural life, religious symbolism, and decorative influences from both folk and Baroque traditions, creating a distinctive visual language that distinguished Moravian households.",
